# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NextSpeak — environment variables
#
# The initial (frontend-only) version of NextSpeak requires NO environment
# variables: it is a static PWA and works with an empty .env.local.
#
# This file documents the OPTIONAL variables that are recognized.
# Copy to `.env.local` only if you need them (`.env.local` is git-ignored —
# never put real secrets in `.env.example` or commit them).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Canonical URL of the deployed site (used for SEO / social-share metadata).
# Defaults to https://nextspeak.vercel.app when unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LEGACY / FUTURE USE ONLY — not used by the current static version.
#
# The original full-stack design (Supabase auth, teacher tokens, certificates)
# is preserved in the first git commit and in `supabase-schema.sql`.
# If a backend phase is revived, it will need these variables:
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_supabase_service_role_key
# JWT_SECRET=generate_with_openssl_rand_base64_32
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
